# S6 load test: {{REPO}} ({{SESSION}})

This is a measured load test of amq-squad, run on the real {{REPO}} repository with real tasks.
Goal: get every task below to an open draft pull request (or an honestly recorded failure) and report.
Nothing is merged by anyone in this squad.

## Facts

- Repository root (lead checkout, team home): `{{ROOT}}`
- Project flag for every amq-squad command: `--project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}}`
- Implementer worktrees (detached, one per implementer): `fullstack` works in `{{ROOT}}/.s6-wt/impl-a`, `backend-dev` works in `{{ROOT}}/.s6-wt/impl-b`.
- Tasks live in the native task store: `amq-squad task list --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}}`. There are {{COUNT}} tasks, titled `<task-id>: <title>` ({{TASKIDS}}). `amq-squad task show <store-id> ...` prints the full brief of a task, including its files, verify command, conflict note and special instructions.
- Baseline: {{BASELINE}}
- Team rules file: `{{ROOT}}/.amq-squad/team-rules.md` (the S6 rules are repeated below and are binding).

{{RULES}}

## Lead (planner, does not implement)

1. Start immediately; do not wait for further instructions. Run `amq-squad task list --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}}` once. The implementers may come up a few minutes after you: if `status` shows them not live yet, dispatch anyway (the durable AMQ mailbox holds the message) or park and re-check on the next wake; never add, start, restart or replace a member yourself.
2. Dispatch one task at a time to each implementer (`fullstack`, `backend-dev`) so both are busy and neither holds more than one task. Use `amq-squad dispatch --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}} --role <role> --task <store-id> --subject "<task-id>: <title>" --body-file <file>` with the task brief (`amq-squad task show <store-id> ...`) saved to a file under your scratchpad.
3. Order: interleave small and medium tasks. Where two tasks list a conflict (see each task's conflict note), give them to different implementers at the same time; do not serialize them to avoid the conflict, the conflict is part of the measurement.
4. When an implementer reports DONE or FAILED, record it, then dispatch the next undispatched task to that implementer. Do a light sanity check only (the PR exists, the verify result is in the PR body). Do not deep-review, do not ask for rework unless the PR is missing or the verify command was not run.
5. You never implement, never merge, never push, never open PRs. If a seat is stuck or blocked on a prompt you cannot resolve, raise a gate to the operator and say so in your summary.
6. When all {{COUNT}} tasks have either a PR or a recorded failure (or the operator tells you to stop), send the operator (`user`) one final AMQ message: a table of task-id, outcome, PR URL or failure reason, and any seat problem you saw. Then idle.
7. Keep your own turns cheap: read `amq-squad status --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}} --json` once per wake, act on one item, then park. Do not poll in a loop.

## Implementers (`fullstack`, `backend-dev`)

For each dispatched task:
1. Claim it if the dispatch has not already (`amq-squad task claim <store-id> --me <your-handle> --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}}`). `task show` gives the full brief.
2. In your own worktree: `git fetch origin main`, then `git switch -c loadtest/<task-id> origin/main`. (Your worktree starts detached; that is expected.)
3. Make the change described by the task, in the listed file(s) only. Follow the neighbouring code's style. Run `gofmt` on what you touched.
4. Run the task's verify command from your worktree root. Fix failures that are in your change. If the verify command cannot pass for a reason outside your change, say so in the PR body.
5. `git add <the task's files>`, commit with message `<task-id>: <title>`, `git push -u origin loadtest/<task-id>`, then `gh pr create --draft --base main --head loadtest/<task-id> --title "[loadtest] <task-id>: <title>" --body-file <file>` where the body contains: what changed, the verify command and its result, and any special-instruction line the task asked for.
6. `amq-squad task done <store-id> --me <your-handle> --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}}`, send the AMQ status message to the lead, then `git switch --detach origin/main` and stop until the next dispatch.
7. Failure path: `amq-squad task fail <store-id> --me <your-handle> --reason "<why>" --project {{ROOT}} --session {{SESSION}}`, send `FAILED: ...`, `git switch --detach origin/main`, stop.
